{
  "summary": "This commit introduces: (1) ReminderService for broadcasting pending task reminders, (2) stuck task detection in Scheduler, (3) dead session cleanup in AgentSessionService, (4) fixes for database connection handling with git branch, and (5) removes redundant `type` column from task INSERTs while keeping the column via migrations as optional with defaults.",
  "learnings": [
    {
      "topic": "Database schema changes",
      "reminder": "When removing a column from INSERTs, either also drop the column in migration OR ensure the column has a DEFAULT value. Don't keep orphaned columns that are never populated."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Migration idempotency",
      "reminder": "Always use IF NOT EXISTS in migrations to handle re-runs. Multiple migrations (053 and 054) both try to add type/category columns - consolidate into one migration."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Process lifecycle",
      "reminder": "When adding new services with setInterval (like ReminderService), always register cleanup in stop() or shutdown hooks to prevent timer leaks."
    },
    {
      "topic": "SQL parameter handling",
      "reminder": "TraeAutoRecoveryService fix: use updated_at (not last_heartbeat_at) when checking task staleness, as last_heartbeat_at may be NULL for older tasks."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Performance consideration",
      "reminder": "DatabaseClient.getGitBranch() runs execSync synchronously on every new connection. Consider caching or making async to avoid blocking connection pool."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Test coverage priority",
      "reminder": "When adding new services (ReminderService), create corresponding test files immediately, not after the fact."
    }
  ],
  "issues": [
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/db/migrations/053_fix_task_type_column.sql & 054_fix_all_missing_columns.sql",
      "issue": "Duplicate migrations both add 'type' and 'category' columns. Should consolidate into single migration.",
      "location": "migrations 053, 054"
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/services/ReminderService.ts",
      "issue": "No test file exists for ReminderService despite being a new critical service.",
      "location": "src/services/ReminderService.ts"
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/db/DatabaseClient.ts:48-56",
      "issue": "getGitBranch() uses synchronous execSync which blocks. Consider making async or caching result.",
      "location": "DatabaseClient.ts:48-56"
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/services/HeartbeatService.ts",
      "issue": "ReminderService.blindLoopTimer never stopped on shutdown. Add to stop() method.",
      "location": "HeartbeatService.ts"
    }
  ],
  "suggestions": [
    {
      "file": "migrations",
      "suggestion": "Merge migrations 053 and 054 into one since they both add the same columns. Use a single migration with 'IF NOT EXISTS' for each column."
    },
    {
      "file": "ReminderService.ts",
      "suggestion": "Add integration test verifying reminder is sent afterDiscussion/Reflection triggers in HeartbeatService."
    },
    {
      "file": "DatabaseClient.ts",
      "suggestion": "Cache git branch result at class level instead of calling execSync on every new connection."
    }
  ],
  "praise": [
    "Stuck task detection in Scheduler is well-designed - checks both started_at (>10min) and updated_at (>5min) to avoid false positives",
    "ReminderService has good UX: cooldown prevents spam, shows top N tasks with priority, reason triggers provide context",
    "cleanup_dead_sessions function properly uses parameterized age_hours for safety",
    "TraeAutoRecoveryService fix correctly uses updated_at instead of last_heartbeat_at which may be NULL"
  ],
  "overallScore": 75,
  "codeQualityScore": 70,
  "testCoverageScore": 60,
  "documentationScore": 80
}
```

